The probability of having k successful trials out of a total of n can be written as the sum
{\displaystyle \Pr(K=k)=\sum \limits _{A\in F_{k}}\prod \limits _{i\in A}p_{i}\prod \limits _{j\in A^{c}}(1-p_{j})}

where 
{\displaystyle F_{k}}

